---
description: Keep application state outside UI components
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

Application state and business logic should live outside UI components using RxJS-based state management.

UI components should consume application state and focus on rendering and user interaction.

Keep purely local UI state inside components when it only affects that component (for example: open/closed state, hover, focus, animation, temporary UI state).

Place shared state and logic in the appropriate common/core workspace when possible.

Only implement separate web or mobile state logic when platform differences require different behavior.